SeaBIOS for the vmd ACPI table loader
=====================================

The stock sysutils/firmware/vmm port configuration in the OpenBSD ports
tree disables CONFIG_FW_ROMFILE_LOAD.  In addition, upstream SeaBIOS only
initializes fw_cfg after recognizing a QEMU PCI host bridge, while vmd uses
its OpenBSD PCHB identity.  Such a firmware image does not read vmd's
etc/table-loader and etc/acpi/rsdp fw_cfg files, so a firmware-booted guest
cannot discover vmd's DSDT, FADT, or MADT.

The config in this directory is the port's minimal vmm configuration with
CONFIG_FW_ROMFILE_LOAD enabled.  CONFIG_ACPI deliberately remains disabled:
the romfile-loader path installs the tables generated by vmd and returns
before SeaBIOS's built-in ACPI generator.  Enabling both is unnecessary and
would leave two components capable of generating the guest's ACPI tables.
The accompanying paravirt patch recognizes the vmd host bridge and permits
SeaBIOS to probe the existing QEMU-compatible fw_cfg interface.

Build through the ports framework so it obtains the supported SeaBIOS source,
SGABIOS source, cross compiler, patches, and packaging layout.  From this
directory, run:

	doas make -C /usr/ports/sysutils/firmware/vmm clean
	doas make -C /usr/ports/sysutils/firmware/vmm \
	    FILESDIR="$PWD" \
	    PATCH_LIST="patch-* $PWD/patch-src_fw_paravirt_c_vmm" build

The resulting firmware is:

	/usr/ports/pobj/vmm-firmware-1.16.3/vmm-bios

The versioned pobj directory follows FW_VER in the port and may change.
Install the test image under a separate name and select it with vmd's `bios`
configuration option before replacing /etc/firmware/vmm-bios system-wide.
